    \end{aligned} \tag{10.11}
    \]
    Because of the equivalence of four atoms per FCC unit cell, the total number of atoms per critical nucleus is just
    \[
    (137\ \text{unit cells/critical nucleus})(4\ \text{atoms/unit cell}) = 548\ \text{atoms/critical nucleus}
    \]
